---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const codeConfig = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "usevyre-context": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@usevyre/mcp-server"]
    }
  }
}`;
---

<DocsLayout title="MCP Server">
  <div class="docs-header">
    <div class="docs-header__meta">
      <span class="vyre-badge vyre-badge--accent">npm</span>
      <span class="vyre-badge vyre-badge--default">v0.1.0</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="docs-title">@usevyre/mcp-server</h1>
    <p class="docs-lead">
      Model Context Protocol server that gives Claude Desktop real-time access to useVyre
      component context — props, valid values, anti-patterns, and examples — without
      copy-pasting anything into your system prompt.
    </p>
  </div>

  <hr class="docs-divider" />

  <h2 class="docs-h2">Setup</h2>
  <p class="docs-p">
    Add to your Claude Desktop config at
    <code>~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json</code>
    (macOS) or <code>%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json</code> (Windows):
  </p>
  <pre class="docs-pre"><code set:text={codeConfig} /></pre>

  <p class="docs-p">Restart Claude Desktop — the server starts automatically on next launch.</p>

  <h2 class="docs-h2">Available tools</h2>
  <p class="docs-p">
    Claude calls these tools automatically when you ask UI-related questions.
    You don't need to invoke them manually.
  </p>

  <div class="docs-table-wrapper">
    <table class="docs-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Tool</th><th>Description</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>get_component_info</code></td>
          <td>Full context for a component — props, valid values, anti-patterns, examples</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>get_valid_props</code></td>
          <td>All valid prop values for a component — called before generating code</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>check_valid_prop_value</code></td>
          <td>Check if a specific prop value is valid — returns valid/invalid + suggestion</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>suggest_component</code></td>
          <td>Suggest the best component(s) for a given use case</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>get_full_context</code></td>
          <td>Complete AI context — all components, tokens, and rules</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>get_anti_patterns</code></td>
          <td>All known hallucination patterns — props and values that don't exist</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>get_version_info</code></td>
          <td>Current schema version and compatible package versions</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 class="docs-h2">How it works</h2>
  <p class="docs-p">
    When you ask Claude to build a UI with useVyre components, it automatically calls
    <code>get_valid_props</code> or <code>get_component_info</code> before writing code —
    so it never guesses prop values.
  </p>

  <div class="docs-callout docs-callout--accent">
    <strong>Example:</strong> Ask Claude <em>"Add a danger button with loading state"</em> —
    it calls <code>get_component_info("Button")</code> and confirms
    <code>variant="danger"</code> and <code>loading</code> are valid before writing the JSX.
  </div>

  <h2 class="docs-h2">Without MCP</h2>
  <p class="docs-p">
    If you prefer not to use MCP, copy the context into your CLAUDE.md manually using
    <a href="/docs/ai-tooling/ai-context-pkg">@usevyre/ai-context</a>. MCP just automates
    this and keeps it always in sync with the installed package version.
  </p>

  <div class="docs-pagination">
    <a href="/docs/ai-tooling/eslint-plugin" class="docs-pagination__link docs-pagination__link--prev">
      ← eslint-plugin-vyre
    </a>
    <span></span>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
